- Story & Context: Written on a rooftop over Spitsbergen as amateur astronomer Greta Lind tracked the trajectory of minor asteroid 433 Eros through a scratched brass reflector. Lind confessed into a cassette recorder that she no longer looked for stars, only for space debris that might smash the seed banks below. Her spoken confession was sampled, pitch-shifted into a dark drill hook, and dropped over a frantic, clawhammer banjo arpeggio. "Fold the tripod before the frost grips the brass," she muttered as the sub-bass threatened to shatter the eyepiece.
